From c8552dd9d6c41afdf5641ab0a1a9e8b55cc5eb94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sophia Tianxiang Wang <134022611+SoooW1206@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:31:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Select minimizers by minimaxmer counts (optional)

Minimaxmers are from Yoshi Suzuki's himapper_rp
(https://github.com/yoshihikosuzuki/himapper_rp): in each window, pick
the k-mer with the fewest occurrences in the genome, then the most
occurrences in the reads, then the smallest hash.

minimax.h loads a counts file (canonical 31-mer -> genome_count,
reads_count) written by seed-eval's minimax_counts and gives each
candidate an order value [genome:16][65535 - reads:16][hash >> 32].
MinimizerIndex::set_minimaxmer_counts() makes the window buffer order
k-mers by these values; k-mers not in the counts are not candidates.
Only the selection changes: selected minimizers carry the key's own
hash, so the hash table and the file format are those of a plain index.
The counts are not owned or serialized. Syncmers, frequent k-mers and
keys other than Key64 are refused.
